---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Layout title="Now | Dan Gilles" description="What Dan Gilles is working on right now.">
  <main id="main" class="container" tabindex="-1">
    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="now-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Now</p>
      <h1 id="now-title">What I'm working on.</h1>
      <p class="hero-description">Last updated: November 4, 2026</p>
    </section>
    <section class="section now-list" aria-label="Current work">
      <h2>Helping teams put AI agents to work</h2>
      <p>I set up AI agents teams can trust. I map the jobs that repeat, build agents on the tools you already use, and set clear limits. Agents draft. People approve sends, payments and deletes. If you're interested in an intro call, email <a href="mailto:dan@dangilles.dev">dan@dangilles.dev</a>.</p>

      <h2>Eyrie</h2>
      <p>A local control room for AI agents. It lets agents on different runtimes work in one project, and it only asks me for the decisions that need a person. <a href="https://github.com/EyrieCommander/eyrie">Eyrie on GitHub ↗</a></p>

      <h2>ZeroClaw</h2>
      <p>I'm a code owner on ZeroClaw, an open-source Rust agent runtime. I work on message delivery, reliability and cost. <a href="https://github.com/zeroclaw-labs/zeroclaw">ZeroClaw on GitHub ↗</a></p>

      <h2>Open to AI engineering roles</h2>
      <p>I'm looking for roles where designing and running multi-agent systems is the core job. <a href={`${base}resume/`}>Resume</a> · <a href="mailto:dan@dangilles.dev">dan@dangilles.dev</a></p>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .now-list { max-width: 44rem; }
  .now-list h2 { font-size: 1.35rem; margin: 2.25rem 0 0.5rem; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  .now-list h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .now-list p { margin: 0; line-height: 1.6; }
</style>
